var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#dev_docs","page":"Developer docs","text":"note: Contributing guidelines\nIf you haven't, please read the Contributing guidelines first.\n\nIf you want to make contributions to this package that involves code, then this guide is for you.","title":"Developer documentation"},{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#First-time-clone","page":"Developer docs","text":"tip: If you have writing rights\nIf you have writing rights, you don't have to fork. Instead, simply clone and skip ahead. Whenever upstream is mentioned, use origin instead.\n\nIf this is the first time you work with this repository, follow the instructions below to clone the repository.\n\nFork this repo\nClone your repo (this will create a git remote called origin)\nAdd this repo as a remote:\ngit remote add upstream https://github.com/thealanjason/GlissADe.jl\n\nThis will ensure that you have two remotes in your git: origin and upstream. You will create branches and push to origin, and you will fetch and update your local main branch from upstream.","title":"First time clone"},{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#Linting-and-formatting","page":"Developer docs","text":"Install a plugin on your editor to use EditorConfig. This will ensure that your editor is configured with important formatting settings.\n\nWe use https://pre-commit.com to run the linters and formatters. In particular, the Julia code is formatted using JuliaFormatter.jl, so please install it globally first:\n\njulia> # Press ]\npkg> activate\npkg> add JuliaFormatter\n\nTo install pre-commit, we recommend using pipx as follows:\n\n# Install pipx following the link\npipx install pre-commit\n\nWith pre-commit installed, activate it as a pre-commit hook:\n\npre-commit install\n\nTo run the linting and formatting manually, enter the command below:\n\npre-commit run -a\n\nNow, you can only commit if all the pre-commit tests pass.","title":"Linting and formatting"},{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#Link-checking-locally","page":"Developer docs","text":"We use lychee for link checking in CI. You can run it locally to avoid waiting for CI. First, install lychee, then run against the repository root using the project config:\n\nlychee --no-progress --config lychee.toml .","title":"Link checking locally"},{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#Testing","page":"Developer docs","text":"As with most Julia packages, you can just open Julia in the repository folder, activate the environment, and run test:\n\njulia> # press ]\npkg> activate .\npkg> test","title":"Testing"},{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#Working-on-a-new-issue","page":"Developer docs","text":"We try to keep a linear history in this repo, so it is important to keep your branches up-to-date.\n\nFetch from the remote and fast-forward your local main\ngit fetch upstream\ngit switch main\ngit merge --ff-only upstream/main\nBranch from main to address the issue (see below for naming)\ngit switch -c 42-add-answer-universe\nPush the new local branch to your personal remote repository\ngit push -u origin 42-add-answer-universe\nCreate a pull request to merge your remote branch into the org main.","title":"Working on a new issue"},{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#Branch-naming","page":"Developer docs","text":"If there is an associated issue, add the issue number.\nIf there is no associated issue, and the changes are small, add a prefix such as \"typo\", \"hotfix\", \"small-refactor\", according to the type of update.\nIf the changes are not small and there is no associated issue, then create the issue first, so we can properly discuss the changes.\nUse dash separated imperative wording related to the issue (e.g., 14-add-tests, 15-fix-model, 16-remove-obsolete-files).","title":"Branch naming"},{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#Commit-message","page":"Developer docs","text":"Use imperative or present tense, for instance: Add feature or Fix bug.\nHave informative titles.\nWhen necessary, add a body with details.\nIf there are breaking changes, add the information to the commit message.","title":"Commit message"},{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#Before-creating-a-pull-request","page":"Developer docs","text":"tip: Atomic git commits\nTry to create \"atomic git commits\" (recommended reading: The Utopic Git History).\n\nMake sure the tests pass.\nMake sure the pre-commit tests pass.\nFetch any main updates from upstream and rebase your branch, if necessary:\ngit fetch upstream\ngit rebase upstream/main BRANCH_NAME\nThen you can open a pull request and work with the reviewer to address any issues.","title":"Before creating a pull request"},{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#Building-and-viewing-the-documentation-locally","page":"Developer docs","text":"Following the latest suggestions, we recommend using LiveServer to build the documentation. Here is how you do it:\n\nRun julia --project=docs to open Julia in the environment of the docs.\nIf this is the first time building the docs\nPress ] to enter pkg mode\nRun pkg> dev . to use the development version of your package\nPress backspace to leave pkg mode\nRun julia> using LiveServer\nRun julia> servedocs()","title":"Building and viewing the documentation locally"},{"category":"section","location":"91-developer/#Making-a-new-release","page":"Developer docs","text":"To create a new release, you can follow these simple steps:\n\nCreate a branch release-x.y.z\nUpdate version in Project.toml\nUpdate the CHANGELOG.md:\nRename the section \"Unreleased\" to \"[x.y.z] - yyyy-mm-dd\" (i.e., version under brackets, dash, and date in ISO format)\nAdd a new section on top of it named \"Unreleased\"\nAdd a new link in the bottom for version \"x.y.z\"\nChange the \"[unreleased]\" link to use the latest version - end of line, vx.y.z ... HEAD.\nCreate a commit \"Release vx.y.z\", push, create a PR, wait for it to pass, merge the PR.\nGo back to main screen and click on the latest commit (link: https://github.com/thealanjason/GlissADe.jl/commit/main)\nAt the bottom, write @JuliaRegistrator register\n\nAfter that, you only need to wait and verify:\n\nWait for the bot to comment (should take < 1m) with a link to a PR to the registry\nFollow the link and wait for a comment on the auto-merge\nThe comment should said all is well and auto-merge should occur shortly\nAfter the merge happens, TagBot will trigger and create a new GitHub tag. Check on https://github.com/thealanjason/GlissADe.jl/releases\nAfter the release is create, a \"docs\" GitHub action will start for the tag.\nAfter it passes, a deploy action will run.\nAfter that runs, the stable docs should be updated. Check them and look for the version number.","title":"Making a new release"},{"category":"section","location":"95-reference/#reference","page":"Reference","text":"","title":"Reference"},{"category":"section","location":"95-reference/#Contents","page":"Reference","text":"Pages = [\"95-reference.md\"]","title":"Contents"},{"category":"section","location":"95-reference/#Index","page":"Reference","text":"Pages = [\"95-reference.md\"]","title":"Index"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.Cache","page":"Reference","text":"            Cache{T,S,W}\n\ncache struct for in-place interpolation on each thread used for parallel execution of the implicit solver.  This structure is of internal use and is not expected to be used outside of the library. \n\nDataTypes\n\nT - Datatype used to store geometry. Should be of type Dual when differentiating with geometry. \nS - Datatype used for indexing. Should be of an integer type. \nW - Datatype used for variables. Should be Dual when differentiation is performed. \n\nFields\n\nids::Vector{S} - Ids to be looked at for interpolation. ids[1] will always be the owner cell index and the other will be the neighbour.\n\nIf ids[2] == ids[1] then the edge is part of boundary. Has a fixed size 2.\n\nparams_central::Vector{T} - Used for storing parameters when performing linear/central interpolation. Has a fixed size 2. \nparams_upwind::Vector{W} - Used for storing parameters when performing first-order upwind interpolation. Has a fixed size 2.\nparams_gamma::Vector{W} - Used for storing parameters when performing the hybrid gamma interpolation. Has a fixed size 2.\nvars_sca::Vector{W} - Used for storing scalar variables when performing interpolation. Has a fixed size 2.\nvars_vec::Vector{Vector{W}} - Used for storing 3D vector variables when performing interpolation. Has a fixed size 2.\nsca_e::Vector{W} - Used for storing the results of a scalar interpolation. Has a fixed size of 1 scalar. \nvec_e::Vector{W} - Used for storing the results of a vector interpolation. Has a fixed size of 1 3D vector.\nIₛ::Matrix{T} - Storage to store curvature transformation. Equals to I - nₚ⊗nₚ\ncoupling::Matrix{T} - Stores transformations to couple owner and neighbour cells. \nvel_i::Vector{W} - Stores the velocity at owner cell. \nvel_n::Vector{W} - Stores the velocity at neighbour cell. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.Cache"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.Cell","page":"Reference","text":"mutable struct Cell{T,S,W}\n\nStructure used for storing geometrical data. \n\nDataTypes\n\nT - Type for numbers for geometrical data. Should be Dual when differentiating with geometry. \nS - Type for integers. Defaults to INT_TYPE\nW - Type for numbers for state variables. Should be Dual when differentiation is performed. \n\nFields\n\nidx::S - Face Index \ncenter::Vector{T} - Coordinates of face centroid \nvertices::Vector{Vector{T}} - Coordinates of the vertices forming the face. \nedge_centers::Vector{Vector{T}} - Coordinates of edge centers of all edges of a face \nedge_lengths::Vector{T} - Edge lengths of all edges of a face \nnormal::Vector{T} - Surface normal at the centroid of a face \narea::T - Area of a face \nedge_binormals::Vector{Vector{T}} - Binormals orthogonal to edges and pointing outwards for each edge of a face \ntransform::Vector{Matrix{T}} - Direction Cosine Matrix for transforming variable of current face for each edge. \ntransform2::Vector{Matrix{T}} - Direction Cosine Matrix for transforming variable of neighbouring face for each edge. \nneighbours::Vector{S} - List of neighbouring faces. \nh::W - Thickness at this cell \nvel::Vector{W} - Velocity (in global coords) in this cell \npb::W - Basal Pressure at this cell \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.Cell"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.Solution","page":"Reference","text":"struct Solution\n\nA Structure containing information to for solution process\n\nArguments\n\nalpha - Pressure Depth Averaged Coefficient. Default is 0.5\nzeta - Velocity Depth Average Coefficient. Default is 1.0\nrho - Material Density (kgm^3). Default is 1500.0\nbasal_stress - Function to compute Momentum Implicit Coefficients for basal stress. \nalpha_p - Under relaxation for pressure. Default is 0.5 \nalpha_u - Under relaxation for velocity. Default is 0.5\nalpha_h - Under relaxation for thickness. Default is 0.5\nMIN_ITERS - Minimum corrections per timestep \nMAX_ITERS - Maximum corrections per timestep \npMAXRESIDUAL - Maximum allowed residual for pressure to exit loop \nhMAXRESIDUAL - Maximum allowed residual for thickness to exit loop \nuMAXRESIDUAL - Maximum allowed residual for velocity to exit loop \nhclip - Clip the thickness to 0 if the value is below `hclip`\nh_min - Minimum thickness to consider a face wet. \nCells - Given by preprocess\npoints - Coordinates of the vertices of a mesh. \nfaces - Connectivities of the vertices of a mesh. \nlocation::String - Location to store the solution in VTK format. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.Solution"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.Solver","page":"Reference","text":"mutable struct Solver{T,S,W}\n\nDataTypes\n\nT - Storage format for numbers related to geometry. Should be Dual when differentiating with geometry\nS - Storage format used for integers. \nW - Storage format for state variables. Should be Dual when differentiation is performed. \n\nFields\n\nalpha_p - Under relaxation for pressure. Default is 0.5 \nalpha_u - Under relaxation for velocity. Default is 0.5\nalpha_h - Under relaxation for thickness. Default is 0.5\nMIN_ITERS - Minimum corrections per timestep. Default is 6\nMAX_ITERS - Maximum corrections per timestep. Default is 15\npMAXRESIDUAL - Maximum allowed residual for pressure to exit loop. Default is 1e-4\nhMAXRESIDUAL - Maximum allowed residual for thickness to exit loop. Default is 1e-4\nuMAXRESIDUAL - Maximum allowed residual for velocity to exit loop. Default is 1e-4\nhclip - Clip the thickness to 0 if the value is below `hclip. Default is0.0`\nh_min - Minimum thickness to consider a face wet. Default is 1e-3\nCells - Given by preprocess\npoints - Coordinates of the vertices of a mesh. \nfaces - Connectivities of the vertices of a mesh. \nlocation::String - Location to store the solution \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.Solver"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.Solver-Tuple{Solution}","page":"Reference","text":"Solver(solution::Solution)\n\nCreate Solver object and fill with default values if solution fields left uninitialized.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.Solver"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.GreenGaussGradient!-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"GreenGaussGradient!(cache, Cells, idx, var, vars)\n\nCompute the gradient using cell-based green gauss gradient scheme. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.GreenGaussGradient!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.MeshQuality-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"MeshQuality(Cells; threads=true)\n\nCompute the orthogonal quality of the mesh. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.MeshQuality"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.RCM-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"RCM(adjgr, degrees)\n\nReverse Cuthill-McKee node-renumbering algorithm.  See also: adjgraph, computeDegrees\n\nArguments\n\nadjgr - Adjacency List of the matrix. Computed using adjgraph\ndegrees - Degrees of each node in the graph. Computed using computeDegrees\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.RCM"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.RCM-Tuple{SparseArrays.SparseMatrixCSC}","page":"Reference","text":"RCM(A::SparseMatrixCSC; sortbydeg = true)\n\nReverse Cuthill-McKee node-renumbering algorithm.\n\nCompute the adjacency graph from a sparse matrix. The sparse matrix A is assumed to be symmetric. The results will be wrong if it isn't.\n\nsortbydeg: Should the neighbor lists be sorted by column degree? The default is true, but often results of very similar quality are obtained when this is set to false and the lists are not sorted. The second option can be much faster, as the sorting is expensive when the neighbor lists are long.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.RCM"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._DCM-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_DCM(local_coords::Vector{Vector{W}})\n\nComputes the Direction Cosine Matrix from local coords to global coords. Equivalent to converting the Vector{Vector} localcoords to Matrix\n\nArguments\n\nlocal_coords::Vector{Vector{Real}} - Local coordinate system of a face\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._DCM"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._areas-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_areas(points::Vector{Vector{W}}, faces::Vector{Vector{S}}, centers::Vector{Vector{W}}) where {W<:Real, S<:Integer}\n\nReturns the areas of all faces of a mesh using the vertices points and the centroids centers.\n\nArguments\n\npoints - Coordinates of all vertices of a mesh \nfaces - Connectivities of all vertices of a mesh \ncenters - Face centroids of all vertices of a mesh \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._areas"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._bi_transforms-NTuple{6, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_bi_transforms(centers::Vector{Vector{W}}, edge_centers::Vector{Vector{W}}, normals::Vector{Vector{W}}, points::Vector{Vector{W}}, faces::Vector{Vector{S}}, neighbours::Vector{Vector{S}}) where {W<:Real, S<:Integer}\n\nReturns the edge binormals and transformation matrices for all faces of a mesh. \n\nArguments\n\ncenters - Face centroids of all faces of a mesh \nedge_centers - Edge centers of all edges of all faces of a mesh \nnormals - Surface normal at face centroids of all faces of a mesh \npoints - Coordinates of all vertices of a mesh \nfaces - Connectivity list of all vertices of a mesh \nneighbours - Adjacency list (neighbour list) of all faces of a mesh\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._bi_transforms"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._center-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_center(points::Vector{Vector{W}}, face::Vector{S}) where {W<:Real, S<:Integer}\n\nComputes the centroid (arithmetic mean) given the vertices and connectivity of a face. \n\nArguments\n\npoints - Coordinates of all vertices of a mesh \nface - Connectivity of a \"face\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._center"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._check_valid_face-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"        _check_valid_face(line)\n\nChecks if the given string line represents a valid face. \n\nArguments\n\nline::String - line which needs to be checked \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._check_valid_face"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._check_valid_int-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"        _check_valid_int(s)\n\nChecks if the given variable is of type-constant INT_TYPE. \n\nArguments\n\ns::AnyDataType - Any Variable \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._check_valid_int"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._cross-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_cross(x::Vector{W},y::Vector{W}) where W<:Real\n\nReturns the cross product of 3D vectors x and y.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._cross"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._dot-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_dot(x::Vector{W},y::Vector{W}) where W<:Real\n\nComputes the dot product (inner product) of 3D vectors x and y.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._dot"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._edge_centers-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_edge_centers(points::Vector{Vector{W}}, faces::Vector{Vector{S}}) where {W<:Real, S<:Integer}\n\nReturns the edge centers for all edges of all faces of a mesh. \n\nArguments\n\npoints - Coordinates of all vertices of a mesh \nfaces - Connecitivity list of vertices of a mesh \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._edge_centers"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._edge_lengths-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_edge_lengths(points::Vector{Vector{W}}, faces::Vector{Vector{S}}) where {W<:Real, S<:Integer}\n\nReturns the edge lengths of all edges of all faces of a mesh. \n\nArguments\n\npoints - Coordinates of all vertices of a mesh\nfaces - Connectivities of all vertices of a mesh \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._edge_lengths"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._local_coords-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_local_coords(n::Vector{W}, p1::Vector{W}, p2::Vector{W}; axis=2) where W<:Real\n\nComputes the local coordinate system given two vertices p1 and p2 and the normal n. \n\nArguments\n\naxis = 2 → The 3D vector p2-p1 is taken to be the y axis of the local coordinate system \naxis = 1 → The 3D vector p2-p1 is taken to be the x axis of the local coordinate system \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._local_coords"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._mag-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_mag(x::Vector{W}) where W<:Real\n\nComputes the Euclidean norm (2-norm) of 3D vector x. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._mag"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._mag2-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_mag2(x::Vector{W},y::Vector{W}) where W<:Real\n\nComputes the Euclidean norm (2-norm) of 3D vector x-y.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._mag2"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._mean_delta-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"computeMeanDelta(Cells)\n\nComputes mean spacing between face centroids. Uses multiple threads if threads=true. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._mean_delta"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._meshcomputations-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_meshcomputations(points, faces, neighbours, mesh)\n\nPrecompute geometrical information of a parsed mesh and store it in the Cell structure\n\npoints - Array containing vertices of the mesh\nfaces - Array containing connectivities/faces of the mesh\nneighbours - Array containing neighbours of each face of the mesh\n\n```\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._meshcomputations"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._ncentroid-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_ncentroid(v1::Vector{W}, v2::Vector{W}, v3::Vector{W}) where W<:Real\n\nReturns the normal to the plane containing 3D vectors v1, v2 and v3 centered at v2.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._ncentroid"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._ncross-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_ncross(x::Vector{W},y::Vector{W}) where W<:Real\n\nExpands to _normalize(_cross(x,y)). Returns the normalized cross product of 3D vectors x and y.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._ncross"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._neighbours-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_neighbours(l, faces)\n\nComputes the neighbours of all faces in the mesh. This algorithm has a time complexity of O(PE) where  P E are the total number of points and edges in the mesh respectively.\n\nArguments\n\nl = P, Total number of points in the mesh\nfaces - Vector containing information of all the faces in the mesh\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._neighbours"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._normalize!-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_normalize!(x::Vector{W}) where W<:Real\n\nNormalizes 3D vector x inplace using its Euclidean norm (2-norm).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._normalize!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._normalize-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_normalize(x::Vector{W}) where W<:Real\n\nReturn 3D vector x normalized using its Euclidean norm (2-norm). \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._normalize"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._normals-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_normals(points::Vector{Vector{W}}, faces::Vector{Vector{S}}) where {W<:Real, S<:Integer}\n\nReturns the face centroid and the surface normal at face centroid. \n\nArguments\n\npoints - Coordinates of the vertices of a mesh \nfaces - Connecitivity list of the vertices of a mesh \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._normals"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._parsefacelabels_openfoam-Tuple{String, Int64}","page":"Reference","text":"_parsefacelabels_openfoam(location_faceLabels, correction_factor)\n\nParse indices of the faces forming the terrain in a text file with OpenFoam format and stores it in INT_TYPE\n\nArguments\n\nlocation_faceLabels::String - location of the facelabels file.\ncorrection_factor::INT_TYPE - remove incorrect entries\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._parsefacelabels_openfoam"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._parsefaces_openfoam-Tuple{String}","page":"Reference","text":"_parsefaces_openfoam(location_faces)\n\nParse the connectivity list of a mesh in an OpenFOAM format and store it in type INT_TYPE\n\nArguments\n\nlocation_faces::String - Location of the \"faces\" file generated by OpenFOAM avalanche module\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._parsefaces_openfoam"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._parsepoints_openfoam-Tuple{String}","page":"Reference","text":"        _parsepoints_openfoam(location_points)\n\nParse the points file generated in an OpenFoam format and stores the coordinates in FLOAT_TYPE format. \n\nArguments\n\nlocation_points::String - Location of the \"points\" file generated by OpenFOAM avalanche module\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._parsepoints_openfoam"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._sum_edges-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Multithreading auxillary for computeMeanDelta\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._sum_edges"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._sum_meandelta-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Multithreading auxillary for computeMeanDelta\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._sum_meandelta"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe._surface_grad!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"_surface_grad!(surface_grad, n)\n\nUpdates the matrix surface_grad inplace using the surface normal n. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe._surface_grad!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.adjMatrix-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"    adjMatrix(neighbours)\n\nComputes the Adjacency Matrix of the Mesh given the neighbours\n\nArguments\n\nneighbours::Vector{Vector{INT_TYPE}} - List of neighbours for each face. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.adjMatrix"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.adjgraph-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"adjgraph(conn, nfens)\n\nCompute the adjacency graph from the array of connectivities of the elements in the mesh.\n\nExample\n\nconn = [9 1 8 4;\n       1 3 2 8;\n       8 2 7 5;\n       2 6 7 7];\nnfens = 9;\nadjgraph(conn, nfens)\n\nshould produce 9-element Array{Array{Int64,1},1}:  [9, 8, 4, 3, 2]  [1, 3, 8, 7, 5, 6]  [1, 2, 8]  [9, 1, 8]  [8, 2, 7]  [2, 7]  [8, 2, 5, 6]  [9, 1, 4, 3, 2, 7, 5]  [1, 8, 4]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.adjgraph"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.adjgraph-Tuple{SparseArrays.SparseMatrixCSC}","page":"Reference","text":"adjgraph(A; sortbydeg)\n\nCompute the adjacency graph from a sparse matrix. \n\nThe sparse matrix A is assumed to be symmetric. The results will be wrong if it isn't.\n\nsortbydeg: Should the neighbor lists be sorted by column degree? The default is true, but often results of very similar quality are obtained when this is set to false and the lists are not sorted. The second option is much faster, as the sorting is expensive.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.adjgraph"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.cellsInsideBoundingPolygon-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"cellsInsideBoundingPolygon(polygon, Cells)\n\nReturns a list of indices of faces lying inside a polygon given by polygon. \n\nArguments\n\npolygon::Vector{Vector{number}} - A list of vertices in order connecting to form a polygon Cells::Vector{Cell{T,S,W}} - Generated by preprocess\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.cellsInsideBoundingPolygon"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.centralInterpolate!-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"centralInterpolate!(Cells, Cell_idx, edge_idx, cache; IDS_PRECOMPUTED, PARAMS_PRECOMPUTED, scalar)\n\nPerforms central interpolation on variables stored in cache.vars_vec if scalar=false or cache.vars_sca if scalar=true\n\nArguments\n\nCells::Vector{Cell{T,S,W}} - Given by preprocess\nCell_idx - Index of Current Face \nEdge_idx - Edge Index \ncache::Cache{T,S,W} - Cache generated for edge interpolation\nIDS_PRECOMPUTED - Skip computation of ids if set true\nPARAMS_PRECOMPUTED - Skip computation of parameters if set true\nscalar - Use cache.vars_sca instead of cache.vars_vec if set true\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.centralInterpolate!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.centralInterpolateParams!-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"centralInterpolateParams!(params, Cells, Cell_idx, edge_idx, ids)\n\nComputes the parameters for central interpolation between edges. \n\nArguments\n\nparams - storage for two values of type FLOAT_TYPE or Dual\nCells::Vector{Cell{T,S,W}} - Given by preprocess\nCell_idx - Index of current cell \nedge_idx - Edge Index \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.centralInterpolateParams!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.checkDry-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"checkDry(solver, ids, idx)\n\nCheck if the face at index idx and it's neighbours are dry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.checkDry"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.computeAverage-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"computeAverage(u)\n\nCompute the arithmetic mean of vector u\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.computeAverage"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.computeChunkAverage-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Multithreading auxillary for computeAverage\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.computeChunkAverage"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.computeDegrees-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"computeDegrees(adjgr)\n\nCompute the degrees of the nodes in the adjacency graph.\n\nArguments\n\nadjgr - Adjacency graph of a matrix. Computed using adjgraph\n\nExample\n\nconn = [9 1 8 4;        1 3 2 8;        8 2 7 5;        2 6 7 7]; nfens = 9; adjgr = adjgraph(conn, nfens) computeDegrees(adjgr)\n\njulia> degrees = computeDegrees(adjgr) 9-element Array{Int64,1}:  5  6  3  3  3  2  4  7  3\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.computeDegrees"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.computeFlux-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Expands to dot(mₑ, vel_edge).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.computeFlux"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.computePressureResidual-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"computePressureResidual(Cells, h, pb, vel, caches; threads=true)\n\nCompute the pressure residual after an iteration. Used mainly for implicit solvers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.computePressureResidual"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.computeResidual-NTuple{6, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"computeResidual(solver, u, u_avg, A, B)\n\nComputes the residual of the linear system Au=B.  See docs for more information about residual calculation.  INTERNAL\n\nArguments\n\nsolver - Solver struct defining the solution process\nu - Current Solution\nu_avg - Average Value of the solution\nA - Coefficient Matrix of the linear system \nB - Source of the linear system \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.computeResidual"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.computeTimeStep-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"computeTimeStep(solver, Cₘ, Δₑ, caches)\n\nCompute the timestep adaptively based on the CFL criterion. dt = Cₘ*Δₑcₑ INTERNAL\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.computeTimeStep"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.compute_chunk_edge_velocity-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Multithreading auxillary for computeTimeStep\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.compute_chunk_edge_velocity"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.convertToMatrix-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"convertToMatrix(a)\n\nConverts a vector vector to a matrix of float type.  The output matrix will be NxM where N = ndims or ncols and M = nrows in the original Vector of Vector a\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.convertToMatrix"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.findRegularPolygon-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"findRegularPolygon(coord_limits; npoints=4, epsilon=1e-1)\n\nReturns a regular polygon within the given constraints: [xmin, xmax, ymin, ymax]. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.findRegularPolygon"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.gamma!-NTuple{7, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"gamma!(cache, Cells, idx, edge_idx, flux_edge, var, vars; βₘ = 0.5, IDS_PRECOMPUTED=false)\n\nPerform gamma interpolation on the var given by var and the total array vars.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.gamma!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.gammaParams!-NTuple{7, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"gammaParams!(cache, Cells, idx, edge_idx, flux_edge, var, vars; βₘ = 0.5)\n\nCompute the parameters for the gamma interpolation scheme. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.gammaParams!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.generateLinearSystem-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Pre-allocate the memory for storing linear systems. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.generateLinearSystem"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.getIds!-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"getIds!(ids, Cells, Cell_idx, edge_idx)\n\nReturns the index of the cells sharing the edge given by Cells[i].edge[edge_idx]\n\nArguments\n\nids - Arrays providing storage for 2 integers of type INT_TYPE\nCells::Vector{Cell{T,S,W}} - Given by preprocess\nCell_idx - Index of current cell \nedge_idx - Edge Index \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.getIds!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.implicit_solve-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"implicit_solve(solver, tspan, Cₘ, saveat, rtol)\n\nThe solver process which simulates the flow. \n\nArguments\n\nsolver - As generated from Solver\ntspan - Flow simulated in the range [tspan[1], tspan[2]]\nCₘ - Maximum courant number allowed. Defaults to 0.9\nsaveat - Save the solution at an equal intervals of saveat. If set to 0.0, no interpolation will be done and original solution returned. \nrtol - Relative tolerance for linear solvers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.implicit_solve"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.init-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"init(plots, threads, stats, float_type, int_type, implicit)\n\nInitialize the library and start PyPlot backend if plots=true\n\nArguments\n\nplots::Bool: toggle side-by-side iteration plotting.\nthreads::Bool: toggle multi-threading\nstats::Bool: toggle debug-printing\nfloat_type::DataType: fallback type for floats.\nint_type::DataType: fallback type for ints.\nimplicit::Bool: whether solve uses the implicit solver. Default true.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.init"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.initWriter-Tuple{String, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"initWriter(location::String, points, faces)\n\nInitialize Writer for VTK files. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.initWriter"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.initializeGeometry-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"initializeGeometry(cells_inside_polygon, Cells, rho; h0 = nothing, u0 = nothing)\n\nInitializes the faces in cells_inside_polygon to have a thickness h0 and velocity u0. Pressure is initialized with a value used for flat surfaces. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.initializeGeometry"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.linearInterpolate!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"linearInterpolate!(out, params, vars)\n\nComputes and stores params[1]*vars[1]+params[2]*vars[2] in out. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.linearInterpolate!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.meshbounds-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"meshbounds(Cells)\n\nComputes the mesh span on the xy plane of mesh cell centroids. See also: preprocess\n\nArguments\n\nCells::Vector{Cell{T,S,W}} - Cell structure generated by preprocess\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.meshbounds"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.meshbounds-Union{Tuple{Array{Vector{T}, 1}}, Tuple{T}} where T<:Real","page":"Reference","text":"meshbounds(points)\n\nComputes the mesh span on the xy plane of mesh vertices. \n\nArguments\n\npoints - Coordinates of all vertices of a mesh. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.meshbounds"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.muIDefault-NTuple{7, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"muIDefault(Cells, h, vel, pb, alpha, zeta, rho, idx)\n\nA default basal stress computation based on muI rheology. INTERNAL\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.muIDefault"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.parsemesh-Tuple{String, String, String}","page":"Reference","text":"parsemesh(location_points, location_faces, location_faceLabels)\n\nParse the files of a mesh in OpenFoam format.\n\nlocation_points::String - Location of \"points\" file generated by OpenFOAM polymesh. \nlocation_faces::String - Location of \"faces\" file generated by OpenFOAM polymesh.\nlocation_faceLabels::String - Location of \"facelabels\" file generated by OpenFOAM polymesh.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.parsemesh"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.preassembleLinearSystem-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"preassembleLinearSystem(Cells::Vector{Cell{T,INT_TYPE,W}}) where {T<:ALLOWED_NUMBERS, W<:ALLOWED_NUMBERS}\n\nGenerate Sparse matrices and their preconditoners with the sparsity pattern of the mesh.  Also allocated additional arrays for solving partial derivatives of linear systems. \n\nArguments\n\nCells::Vector{Cell{T,INT_TYPE,W}} - Discretized Geometry\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.preassembleLinearSystem"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.preprocess-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"preprocess(points, faces; comp_neighbours=true)\n\nPrecompute geometrical information and store it in the Cell structure. \n\npoints - coordinates of the vertices of the mesh. \nfaces - connectivity list of the mesh. \nW - Datatype to be used for variables. Should be of type Dual if differentiating with geometry\ncomp_neighbours - Whether to compute neighbours or read from file. Default is true. In case of incompatibility with mesh, neighbours will be recomputed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.preprocess"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.relax!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"relax!(var_new, var_old, alpha)\n\nUnder relax the field stored in var_new with the old field var_old inplace. alpha controls the amount of relaxation and should be in the range 01\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.relax!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.relaxMomentum!-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"relaxMomentum!(A,B,alpha,vel0,Cells)\n\nUnder-relax the linear system for momentum equation in-place. Equation Under-relaxation. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.relaxMomentum!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.relaxThickness!-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"relaxThickness!(A,B,alpha,h0,Cells; threads=true)\n\nUnder relax the linear system for the continuity (thickness) equation in-place. Equation Under-relaxation. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.relaxThickness!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.repack-Union{Tuple{D}, Tuple{Vector{D}, Any}} where D","page":"Reference","text":"Repack the computed values and partial derivatives for solution of a linear system.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.repack"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.resetCells-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"resetCells(Cells) where {T<:Real, S<:Integer}\n\nReset discretized geometry's stored information to zero. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.resetCells"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.saveAt-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Save the solution at prescribed timesteps.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.saveAt"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.saveSolution-Tuple{String, Vararg{Any, 6}}","page":"Reference","text":"saveSolution(location::String, time, time_steps, sol, iter, points_mat, cells)\n\nSave the solution at the time time. See also: writeToVTK\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.saveSolution"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.scalingFactor-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"scalingFactor(solver, p)\n\nReturns the scaling factor for scaling the pressure equation residual. INTERNAL\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.scalingFactor"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.solveLinearSystem-NTuple{11, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Solves the linear system and computes its partial derivatives\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.solveLinearSystem"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.sum_dry-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Multithreading auxillary for totalDryCells.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.sum_dry"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.testInside-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"testInside(coords, bounding_coords)\n\nTests whether a point with coordinates coords is inside the region given by bounding_coords: [xmin, xmax, ymin, ymax] INTERNAL\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.testInside"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.totalDryCells-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"totalDryCells(solver)\n\nCompute the total number of dry cells at any time step. See also: checkDry. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.totalDryCells"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.updateMomentum!-NTuple{13, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"updateMomentum!(solver, Av, Bv, precon_v, dt, t, p, vel0, h0, caches; threads=true, prev_solution=nothing, pprev_solution=nothing)\n\nSolves the momentum equation inplace and stores the result in vel0. INTERNAL\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.updateMomentum!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.updateSol!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Update function to store the solution after a time-step.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.updateSol!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.updateThickness!-NTuple{12, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"updateThickness!(solver, Ah, Bh, precon_h, dt, t, p, vel, h0, caches; threads=true, prev_solution=nothing, pprev_solution=nothing)\n\nSolves the continuity (thickness) equation inplace and stores the result in h0. INTERNAL\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.updateThickness!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.upwindInterpolate!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"upwindInterpolate!(cache, flux_edge; PARAMS_PRECOMPUTED, scalar)\n\nPerform upwind interpolation using cache.vars_vec if scalar=false and cache.vars_sca if scalar=true\n\nArguments\n\ncache::Cache{T,S,W} - Cache for edge interpolation\nflux_edge::W - Flux at edge (computed using central interpolation)\nPARAMS_PRECOMPUTED - Skip computation of params if set true\nscalar - Use cache.vars_vec if set to false, else use cache.vars_sca\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.upwindInterpolate!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.upwindParams!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"upwindParams!(params, flux_edge)\n\nCompute Upwind Interpolation parameters based on flux at edge. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.upwindParams!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.writeFileToVTK-Tuple{String, Vararg{Any, 4}}","page":"Reference","text":"writeFileToVTK(filename::String, sol, idx, points_mat, cells)\n\nWrite a file with a given filename and sol to disk in Paraview's VTK format.  See also: writeToVTK\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.writeFileToVTK"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.writeToVTK-Tuple{String, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"writeToVTK(location::String, sol, points, faces)\n\nWrite a solution to VTK files at the given location. \n\nArguments\n\nlocationString : Destination of the VTK files \nsol : Solution from the solver's output \npoints : Mesh vertices \nfaces : Mesh connectivities\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.writeToVTK"},{"category":"macro","location":"95-reference/#GlissADe.@maybe_threads-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"maybe_threads(flag::Bool, expr)\n\nExecute a for-loop with threads only if flag==true\n\nExample Usage\n\njulia> @maybe_threads (1==2) for i in 1:10\n        println(\"I love Julia!\")\n       end \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlissADe.@maybe_threads"},{"category":"section","location":"90-contributing/#contributing","page":"Contributing guidelines","text":"First of all, thanks for the interest!\n\nWe welcome all kinds of contribution, including, but not limited to code, documentation, examples, configuration, issue creating, etc.\n\nBe polite and respectful, and follow the code of conduct.","title":"Contributing guidelines"},{"category":"section","location":"90-contributing/#Bug-reports-and-discussions","page":"Contributing guidelines","text":"If you think you found a bug, feel free to open an issue. Focused suggestions and requests can also be opened as issues. Before opening a pull request, start an issue or a discussion on the topic, please.","title":"Bug reports and discussions"},{"category":"section","location":"90-contributing/#Working-on-an-issue","page":"Contributing guidelines","text":"If you found an issue that interests you, comment on that issue what your plans are. If the solution to the issue is clear, you can immediately create a pull request (see below). Otherwise, say what your proposed solution is and wait for a discussion around it.\n\ntip: Tip\nFeel free to ping us after a few days if there are no responses.\n\nIf your solution involves code (or something that requires running the package locally), check the developer documentation. Otherwise, you can use the GitHub interface directly to create your pull request.","title":"Working on an issue"},{"category":"section","location":"#GlissADe","page":"GlissADe","text":"Documentation for GlissADe.","title":"GlissADe"},{"category":"section","location":"#Contributors","page":"GlissADe","text":"<!-- ALL-CONTRIBUTORS-LIST:START - Do not remove or modify this section -->\n<!-- prettier-ignore-start -->\n<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n<!-- markdownlint-restore -->\n<!-- prettier-ignore-end -->\n\n<!-- ALL-CONTRIBUTORS-LIST:END -->","title":"Contributors"}]
}
